# ---------------- Arcade_Enemy.events (Task 7 Part G3 + G4 phase 1) ----------------
# No NavMesh, no rays, no waypoints: walk straight at the player on the floor, swing on contact.
# This is the Double Dragon / Contra shape — one polled steering line plus a melee `near`, and
# a spawner (Arcade_Spawner.events) refills the lane.
#
# Phase 1 (knockdown & combo): `my state` is the switch. Walking and swinging only run in
# "walk"; a hit flips the enemy to "down" for 0.4 s, then "getup" for 0.2 s, then back to
# "walk" and one point of Combo. A hit that lands while already down costs health but does not
# restart the wait blocks (`my state is not "down"` gates the flip), so a burst cannot stack
# stuns. Combo's decay lives on the spawner, which is one actor — in a shared sheet every clone
# would decay the same global.
#
# SETUP (editor): the scene's `Arcade_Enemy` actor is the spawn template — give it an EventSheet
# with Event File = Arcade_Enemy, a BoxCollider, and leave the actor inactive. `spawn Arcade_Enemy
# at SpawnAhead` clones it activated; the clone keeps the template's name (Flax allows duplicate
# actor names), so this one sheet drives every enemy on the floor.
#
# No NavMesh bake is involved: `move toward` is a direct vector, the same word the Variant 1
# chase uses. It walks into walls rather than around them — the documented con of the variant.

when me appears
  enemy type "Zombie"
  set state walk
  print "Arcade_Enemy: walking in"

when every 0.2 seconds
  my state is "walk"                  # a downed enemy neither walks nor swings
  move toward player speed 60         # re-issued so it tracks a moving player
  # loop anim "Walk"                 # simple meshes have no clips; armature enemies can

when me is near player by 1.5
  my state is "walk"
  my Hostile is true
  # play anim "Attack"
  send message "hurt" to nearest player

# ---- taking a shot ----
# TK_Bullet.events reacts to actors named `Enemy`; the lane names its enemy `Arcade_Enemy`, so
# the hit lands from this side instead: a shot that overlaps costs 10 of the zombie's 50 and is
# used up. Same idea as Enemy.events' damage block, just keyed on the shot rather than a message,
# because a lane full of clones has no single `Enemy` actor to message.
# The damage lands either way; only the knockdown is gated, so a burst still hurts a downed enemy.
when me touches Bullet
  add -10 to my Health
  destroy other
  my state is not "down"
  set state down

# ---- a melee hit from the player (the phase-1 stun entry the listing describes) ----
when message "hurt" arrives
  my state is not "down"
  set state down

# ---- the knockdown itself: down 0.4 s, get up 0.2 s, then walk and count the combo hit ----
when state is down
  print "Arcade_Enemy: knocked down"
  wait 0.4 seconds
  my state is "down"                  # still down (not re-flipped)? stand up
  set state getup
  wait 0.2 seconds
  my state is "getup"                 # not re-hit during the stand-up? back to the lane
  set state walk
  add 1 to Combo

when my Health becomes 0
  add 1 to kills my Type
  add -1 to EnemiesAlive
  # play anim "Die"
  destroy me
